# LoCoMo single-hop control set (30 questions).
#
# Stores only IDs and selection metadata. Question text and gold data are read from
# `dataset/locomo-refined/` at runtime.
#
# Purpose: provide questions that should answer correctly from one lookup, using the
# same conversations as `coq-multihop.jsonl`. This separates useful multi-hop behavior
# from unnecessary extra retrieval.
#
# Selection is deterministic:
# 1. Use conversations conv-26, conv-30, and conv-41.
# 2. Require exactly one dialogue evidence ID.
# 3. Use non-empty answers from categories 2 (temporal), 3 (open), and 4 (single-hop).
# 4. Keep evidence rounds distinct and rotate categories.
# 5. Exclude `conv-41#q0033`: its answer exists only in an image, so it is not
#    recoverable from the indexed text.
#
# LoCoMo evidence IDs identify a session entry point, not necessarily the exact
# supporting turn. The selection criterion therefore applies at session scope.
#
# These questions should route as `DEFAULT`; routing them to the multi-hop path is a
# regression signal.
